      en: ["Opened to the public in 1961 in the capital, Kingston.", "Part of a larger 200-acre Royal Botanical Gardens estate.", "Sanctuary for the endangered Jamaican Iguana (Cyclura collei).", "Home to over 60 different species of native and exotic animals.", "The site was originally a 17th-century sugar plantation.", "Educational programs reach thousands of students annually."],
